📚UNDER THE COVER WITH PETRA COLLINS 🩷 Discover the books and images that have informed @petrafcollins unique visual language and the making of her newly published photo book STAR! 

Revisiting the books that captured her imagination as a teenager, like the Corinne Day photos from the set of The Virgin Suicides and the 1977 idol book dedicated to The Runaways, Collins speaks to how discovering these images on Tumblr opened up an entirely new visual universe to her. 

Behind the scenes of STAR, she reflects on the spectacle of fame and how it can feel both intoxicating and suffocating. Drawing inspiration from her own work with pop stars alongside these early references, her approach to photography is distinctly cinematic, weaving narrative, mood, and costuming as though composing scenes from a non-existent film. 

